sequenceDiagram
  %% status: draft
  %% command: proof:pool:drain
  %% kind: proof.pool.drain
  autonumber
  participant CLI as Operator<br/>CLI · MCP
  participant GW as Gateway
  participant SW as Swamp
  participant CP as CI Nodes<br/>warm copies
  CLI->>GW: Drain the warm pool
  %%> Why:
  %%> - A maintenance window that needs every copy of the proof Project's default gone runs this one command.
  GW->>GW: Record the drain
  %%> The drain is a Gateway record. It lasts until proof:pool:resume, across Gateway restarts. While it holds, no refill starts a warm copy. The drain is recorded under the lock of the proof default, which a refill takes again before it starts a copy: a refill whose reads ran during the drain starts none, and copies that a refill started before the drain are cancelled next.
  GW->>GW: Cancel each idle warm copy
  %%> Idle: no proof has taken it. Each cancel destroys the copy through its task group, as for any proof copy, with discard. A warm copy whose create still runs is cancelled the same way: the group's cancel waits for the create to end.
  %%> Running proofs:
  %%> - A proof's copies, also those taken from the pool, are not touched. Each is destroyed at its run's end, as always.
  GW-->>CLI: Drained<br/>warm copies being destroyed
  %%> The answer names the warm copies whose destroy started and the proof copies that still run. The operator waits for both lists to end: proof:pool:drain again shows them.
  SW->>CP: Destroy each warm copy<br/>release its hold
  %%> The copy's destroy drops its hold on the Node's places. The destroy of the last copy on a Node starts the runners that the holds stopped.
